sentences.l:
And she found Telemachus and Nestor's splendid son
sleeping in the fore-house of Menelaus, glorious,
the son of Nestor, indeed, by soft sleep overcome;

and I feel indignation at any other, too,
a man who receives guests, who beyond measure welcomes,
and beyond measure hates;

And if you wish to turn through Hellas and mid-Argos,
so that I myself may follow you, and I shall yoke the horses beneath for you,
and the towns of men I shall lead you to;
